    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:filefetcher:0012:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:filefetcher:0012",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "A `FileFetcher` can also be used standalone in your scripts to efficiently fetch remote content in background threads.",
      "normalizedSource": "A `FileFetcher` can also be used standalone in your scripts to efficiently fetch remote content in background threads.",
      "sourceHash": "b8e8202a16acbd1861c3ae4ae476f119ff0f85ec836cec1d669f924af58c8daf",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Start prefetching these files.",
      "contextAfter": "```\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom mlx.data.core import AWSFileFetcher\n\nLOCAL_CACHE = Path(\"/path/to/local/cache\")\n\nff = AWSFileFetcher(\n    \"my-cool-bucket\",\n    endpoint=\"https://my.endpoint.com/\"\n    local_prefix=LOCAL_CACHE,\n    num_kept_files=100,\n)\n\n# When fetch returns my/remote/path/foo.npy will be in LOCAL_CACHE\nff.fetch(\"my/remote/path/foo.npy\")\nassert (LOCAL_CACHE / \"my/remote/path/foo.npy\").is_file()\n\n# We can prefetch in the background\nff.prefetch([\"foo_1.npy\", \"foo_2.npy\"])\nff.fetch(\"foo_1.npy\")\n# process foo_1 while foo_2 downloads in the background\n```",
      "documentTitle": "Miscellaneous",
      "framework": "MLX",
      "ko": "",
